From 2cd2eafcdeafe2f9500a70b79065afcedaa8d13c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patch-author <a@a.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 07:15:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Patch 0376: DLC ownership backed by the real Steam SDK, not
 file presence

- electron/main.ts: DLC_APP_IDS map (founders_pack: 5256720, the real
  registered App ID), new steam:isDlcOwned IPC handler calling
  steamClient.apps.isDlcInstalled(). Returns null (not false) whenever
  Steam genuinely can't answer -- only an explicit true/false is treated
  as authoritative.
- preload.ts / SaveManager.ts: isDlcOwned exposed on the littleKnight
  bridge, same null-vs-boolean contract documented at both call sites.
- DlcManager.ts: loadInstalledPacks now checks Steam ownership FIRST for
  each pack -- an explicit false skips it entirely without even
  attempting to fetch pack.json (closes the actual gap: nothing
  previously stopped a non-owner's disk from having a stray pack.json
  and being treated as owning it). true or null both fall through to
  the existing file-presence fetch, so dev/testing without Steam running
  is unaffected.
- Found and documented, not fixed here: public/dlc/founders_pack/
  pack.json gets bundled INSIDE the base app's own app.asar during vite
  build, confirmed via npx asar list -- a Steam depot split alone can't
  fix this, since the file is already sealed into the base bundle before
  Steam is involved. Deliberately deferred (discussed and confirmed
  before proceeding) -- the actual grant is already correctly gated by
  real ownership regardless, so this is a content-exposure gap, not a
  functional one.
- Verified: tsc --noEmit, vite build, electron-builder --linux dir
  package build, a real launch under xvfb-run confirming no crash from
  the new IPC path, and four scripted ownership scenarios (mocked fetch
  + mocked isDlcOwned) covering no-bridge/false/true/null.
